From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shawn Zhang <shawn.zhang@pepperstone.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 14:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Disable SSL session cache for realtime cert policy

Vanadium denylist / whitelist pins / cert_monitor run in
ssl_client_socket_impl after certificate verification. Chromium already
sets SSL_CTX_set_reverify_on_resume(1), so resumed sessions re-verify.
Still disable SSLClientSessionCache entirely so every new socket does a
full handshake path and cannot reuse a cached TLS session ticket.

HTTP disk cache is a separate concern (no network ⇒ no TLS). Prefer
disabling HTTP cache at the browser layer or hard-refresh when testing
policy changes.

diff --git a/net/http/http_network_session.cc b/net/http/http_network_session.cc
index 1111111111111..2222222222222 100644
--- a/net/http/http_network_session.cc
+++ b/net/http/http_network_session.cc
@@ -147,7 +147,14 @@
       proxy_resolution_service_(context.proxy_resolution_service),
       ssl_config_service_(context.ssl_config_service),
       http_auth_cache_(
           params.key_auth_cache_server_entries_by_network_anonymization_key),
-      ssl_client_session_cache_(SSLClientSessionCache::Config()),
+      ssl_client_session_cache_([] {
+        SSLClientSessionCache::Config config;
+        // Vanadium: no TLS session tickets/cache. Forces a handshake (and
+        // therefore cert verify + downstream policy checks) on each new
+        // socket instead of resuming a prior session.
+        config.max_entries = 0;
+        return config;
+      }()),
       ssl_client_context_(context.ssl_config_service,
                           context.cert_verifier,
                           context.transport_security_state,
                           &ssl_client_session_cache_,
                           context.sct_auditing_delegate),
